Z||000000||PearlBlueSoul||11-29-2000||04:07 PM||||Stupid question, but my queries will get better as I get more familiar with fieros and this board.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  learn who's who, who's the vets and what not.  <P>How well are you taking this new adjustment to having 2 people on your board?  seems everyone's taking it very well...but I'm sure there are a few who might like to ask something of me.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Just curious to know if there's anythin' I can do to make this better somehow.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  always lookin' to lend a hand.<P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.atlantamr2s.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/darionscard</A>  <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">       <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.||||reg||1
Z||000001||william_thorniii||11-29-2000||05:33 PM||||PBS,<P>It it fairly simple to see who are the vets.  Date of registration and number of posts are clearly stated.  <P>That aside, I don't think any of us have problems with you.  You have represented your group well.  We (Fiero owners) have a tendency to be the hot-headed ones.  If you want to see a hot thread, perform a search for a thread about spark plugs contributed to by a gentleman named "Vinny Wolf" or some derivation of that name or another search by a member named "needle".  Some people just want to stir things up and we respond rather quickly.  <P>The most specialized folks on the forum would probably be:<P>theogre: Electrical wizard and Ruler of DIS Duke Fiero's<P>Will:  Will is a recent addition, but is all about sleepers and suspensions.  It is all go and no show with this guy.<P>Phil:  Phil has participated in two (or is it three) consecutive Hot Rod Power Tours.  He has a 3800 series II sc engine in the back of his little yellow formula.  <P>MWS: Michael W. Smith (I kid you not) is very intelligent in the specialities of suspensions and the TDC swap.  Unfortunately he is not on the Forum.<P>1fst2m6 (Travis) and Hypnotise (Marc): Are both NOS guys.  Marc just custom fabbed some unbelieveable exhaust for his impressive new engine.  Travis is our dyno king down at <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  and is always looking for that little extra power.  <P>terryk:  Terry is amazing.  He is a chip burning, fuel mapping and all around ECM genius.<P>Mr. Cliff Pennock:  Cliff in addition to being an electrical genius soon to be selling an electronic dash for the Fiero, he is the creator/moderator/owner/lord of this bulletin board.  It is not the oldest, nor the largest on-line Fiero community, but it is certainly the best.  Most of us in here have been booted off at least one of the many lists out there (I have been booted from 2 different lists and one of those booted me twice).  <BR>There really are too many guys on this board that constantly astound me with knowledge.  <P>Then there are the vendors:<P>archie: V8Archie is the purveyor of sbc engine conversion kits and more recently Candy Apple Cars body kits<P>rodney dickman: The Getrag guy and purveyor of miscellaneius Fiero bracketry and cosmetic items<P>Mr. Ed Parks (The Fiero Factory): In my opinion Ed is the absolute supreme lord over all stock Fiero's and the pushrod 3.4L engine swap. <P>The Fiero Shop:  George Miller owns the shop and Terry Owens works/lives there.  These guys are a great source of parts and repair.  They sell some of the best Fiero clutches on the market out there.  <P>007Doug:  Doug Kinney runs the Fiero Warehouse.  He has lots of miscellaneous factory parts at great prices.  <P>Kick Hill Farms:  Part supplier to the NE Fiero community.  <P>mrfiero:  Mike Valentine has recently begun a business specializing in the 1988 model year Fiero.  He has a couple of very nice models himself.<P>fierodave: Purveyor of typically entire cars, but has recently delved deep into the world of Fiero parts with an enormous acquisition of Fiero related remains and goodies out in Cali somewhere.<P>Paul McKibben: Paul sells us great replacements for our sail panels and some custom graphics.<P>Dave K.: Dave knows/has/sells all Fiero related literature.<P>IRM:  Sells the unbelieveable IMSA DGP body work that is similar to the bodies sanctioned for IMSA racing.  <P>The Fiero Store:  These guys dabble in just about everything Fiero.<P>FOCOA:  Don't know too much about them, but know that they deal extensively with Fiero's.<P>Ryanne Motorsports: Until recently, Ryane was a supplier of unbelieveable fiero suspension upgrades.  <P>There are many more too.  This just gives you an idea of some of the unbelieveable support we have in our community.  With this group of folks and suppliers there really isn't anything one can't do.  <P><BR>I am sure that I left many great folks out.  I did not intend to... so if I left you out, I apologize.  Pipe up and I will add you to my personal list :~p<BR>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever2||11-29-2000||05:57 PM||||I'm a list-maker.  Most recently of 2001 Fiero shows & events, and Fiero club websites.  I have nothing to contribute technically, but make erratic attempts at humor.  I have way too much time on my hands and watch this board almost round the clock, so my post count has been growing quickly.  Usually I don't think before I hit the Submit button, like now.<P>I have a question for PBS... do you MR2 guys hate ricers too?  Or do you even know what that means?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||PearlBlueSoul||11-29-2000||06:09 PM||||Oh hell yes!  Man, we had a whole thread about that!  ugh..we HATE ricers, and scoff at their attempts to be fast.  <P>All of us, MKI n/As included, are fully aware that 9 times out of 10 we can blow the DOORS off anything that is rice.  I have done this multiple times (and hope to do it many more.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)  hehe.  Belive me, someone who rices out a MR2 is greatly scoffed and re-scoffed.  We just put it this way, "such a brilliant car shouldn't be given to stupid people."  We don't want people to have a MR2 if they won't care for it, and if they truly don't understand what a unique and wonderful car it is their driving.<P>I should assume you guys feel the same to some degree.<P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.atlantamr2s.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/darionscard</A>  <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">       <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever2||11-29-2000||06:18 PM||||<B>NOW</B> I will welcome you without reservation! *virtual handshake* <P>eh, sorry about that "manuals translated badly" crack on that other topic earlier.<P>Mid-engine two-seaters without cupholders rule!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||RiceCooker||11-29-2000||06:18 PM||||You betcha||||reg||6
